  "term": "criminal responsibility",
  "definition": "Criminal responsibility is the legal question of whether a person can be held answerable for a crime, especially in relation to insanity. In this historical account, a person who becomes insane after the act may be barred from pleading, trial, judgment, or execution until mentally fit, because they cannot properly take part in their defence.",
